#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Allowlisting gateway in front of the croit API.

croit's admin token can do far more than a portal needs (certificates, servers,
API tokens, ...). This gateway holds the real token and forwards only the
(method, path) pairs that Bucketeer's CroitClient uses; everything else gets
403. Clients authenticate to the gateway with a separate client token, so a
compromised client never learns the real one.

Standard library only; needs Python 3.9+ (checked at startup). It is not part of Bucketeer: it never
imports it, and Bucketeer never imports it.

Run it as a different Unix user than the client, and keep its environment file
readable only by that user. Point the client's CROIT_URL at
http://127.0.0.1:18089/api and its CROIT_API_TOKEN at the client token.

Environment:
  CROIT_URL               croit API base URL, e.g. https://croit.example.org/api
  CROIT_API_TOKEN         the real croit token (required); never leaves the gateway
  CROIT_CA_CERT_FILE      CA bundle for the croit endpoint
  CROIT_TLS_VERIFY        set to false to skip croit TLS verification
  CROIT_GATE_LISTEN       host:port to listen on (default 127.0.0.1:18089)
  CROIT_GATE_CLIENT_TOKEN token clients must send as a Bearer token (required,
                          at least 32 characters, different from CROIT_API_TOKEN)
  CROIT_GATE_TIMEOUT      seconds per upstream request, and the total time a client
                          has to send its request (default 30)
  CROIT_GATE_MAX_CONNECTIONS
                          concurrent client connections; more get 503 (default 64)

Install (as the gateway's own Unix user, no root needed):
  croit-gate install [--enable]
    Copies this script to ~/.local/bin/croit-gate (0755), writes the systemd
    user unit ~/.config/systemd/user/croit-gate.service, and writes an env
    template ~/.config/croit-gate/env (0600) ONLY if none exists (an existing
    env file and its tokens are never touched). Re-running it updates the
    script and the unit. It then prints the remaining steps. With --enable it
    also runs `systemctl --user daemon-reload` and `enable --now`; without it,
    it runs no systemctl at all.

Options:
  --check          validate the configuration, call GET /auth/token-info
                   upstream, and exit (0 ok, 1 error)
  --allow-remote   allow a non-loopback CROIT_GATE_LISTEN address. The
                   gateway speaks plain HTTP: anyone who can sniff or reach
                   that address can use the client token. Only do this on a
                   trusted, isolated network.

Exit codes: 0 success, 1 error, 2 usage error.
"""

